      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 6.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Okay, so hello doctor, sorry, am I early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.07,
      "end_seconds": 12.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.73,
      "end_seconds": 16.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "It's a weak urine stream, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.35,
      "end_seconds": 20.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.38,
      "end_seconds": 26.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Okay, so I've had it for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.5,
      "end_seconds": 29.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.28,
      "end_seconds": 49.88,
      "duration_seconds": 19.6,
      "text": "right, it feels mild to me i mean, as for dribbling at the end, I honestly can't say when that began it might have been last month or the month before about dribbling at the end, I'd say severe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.96,
      "end_seconds": 55.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Have you had to to have anything operated on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.44,
      "end_seconds": 67.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Uh, just a a stent put in my heart, two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.68,
      "end_seconds": 83.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Have you got any chronic problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.06,
      "end_seconds": 103.9,
      "duration_seconds": 19.84,
      "text": "I have diabetes, for two years. High blood pressure, for about a year. I mean, I have an enlarged prostate, for five years. It's the not knowing that gets to me. I, I have heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.04,
      "end_seconds": 113.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "alright, high blood pressure and an enlarged prostate, that matches what I have here. Okay, what about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.26,
      "end_seconds": 119.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.85,
      "end_seconds": 123.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.97,
      "end_seconds": 129.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.84,
      "end_seconds": 135.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Do you exercise at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.05,
      "end_seconds": 142.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "I go to the gym a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.56,
      "end_seconds": 145.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Are you living with family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.22,
      "end_seconds": 150.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I stay with my daughter and her family"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.8,
      "end_seconds": 152.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "And your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.16,
      "end_seconds": 158.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I drive a delivery van all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.95,
      "end_seconds": 164.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Okay, anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.76,
      "end_seconds": 169.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "uh, my mother has migraines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.67,
      "end_seconds": 174.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Tell me what you take day to day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.37,
      "end_seconds": 184.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "I'm on Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day. So, I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.16,
      "end_seconds": 185.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.81,
      "end_seconds": 193.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Right, I take tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.03,
      "end_seconds": 197.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.16,
      "end_seconds": 203.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Yes, peanuts, it gives me my lips swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.35,
      "end_seconds": 224.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "And And what about back pain or burning when passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.51,
      "end_seconds": 229.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "No, um, not any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.48,
      "end_seconds": 235.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "okay, and what about blood in the urine or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.9,
      "end_seconds": 240.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "No, no blood in the urine or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.4,
      "end_seconds": 245.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "on the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.24,
      "end_seconds": 251.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.47,
      "end_seconds": 255.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "can I take your vitals now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.31,
      "end_seconds": 267.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "One second..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.45,
      "end_seconds": 293.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 117 over 70, SpO2 98 percent on room air, pulse is 78 beats a minute. And temperature 36.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.33,
      "end_seconds": 297.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'd like to examine you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.96,
      "end_seconds": 300.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "No problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.78,
      "end_seconds": 304.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "hold that position for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.32,
      "end_seconds": 315.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "your bladder isn't palpable and the tummy is soft"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.04,
      "end_seconds": 319.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Take your time, no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.55,
      "end_seconds": 339.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "On rectal examination the prostate feels smooth and enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.85,
      "end_seconds": 342.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "no problem"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.02,
      "end_seconds": 347.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Good, that's the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.52,
      "end_seconds": 376.72,
      "duration_seconds": 20.2,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, it points towards an enlarged prostate causing urinary symptoms. Another possibility is a bladder problem. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had a weak urine stream for about a year, mild, and no burning when passing urine or blood in the urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.9,
      "end_seconds": 380.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "yes, um, that's right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.39,
      "end_seconds": 403.85,
      "duration_seconds": 22.46,
      "text": "I think kidney function tests makes sense here, for urinary symptoms. I'll request an ultrasound of the bladder and prostate, it'll help with urinary symptoms. I think a PSA test makes sense here, for urinary symptoms. Cut back on tea and and coffee after the afternoon and go before you sleep."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 404.42,
      "end_seconds": 409.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Do I need a urine test? I read it might help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.67,
      "end_seconds": 425.48,
      "duration_seconds": 14.81,
      "text": "Alright, not at this point, no. It isn't indicated yet. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 426.73,
      "end_seconds": 430.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Alright, I know what to look for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.44,
      "end_seconds": 440.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "please come and see me after the results are back take care, and call us if anything changes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.95,
      "end_seconds": 446.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I appreciate it, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 447.57,
      "end_seconds": 448.27,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ]
